# What a mob's clone gets (#66). In the temple (3001), Smokegod (60) and Seraph (56).
# - Smokegod has Hassan wield a glowing long sword (3349: hitroll +2, damroll +2), blesses him (hitroll and saves),
#   stats him, and clones him. The clone goes first in the room, so it's 1.hassan. Stock copied Hassan's hitroll,
#   damroll and saves, which already had the sword's and bless's in them, then added bless again: the clone had bless
#   twice. Now it gets Hassan's own values, bless once and the sword equipped, so it matches Hassan, and removing the
#   sword takes each of them to the same values.
# - Smokegod gives a cityguard (3060) a ring of protection (3043: armor -2, saves -1), sets its cost to 2000 (too much
#   for Seraph to clone at trust 55) and her trust to 55, and Seraph clones the guard. Stock's clone kept the ring's
#   armor and saves without the ring: its worn objects were copied as worn but never equipped, and their bonuses came
#   with the guard's values. Now the clone has the guard's values without the ring, and it has no ring to remove.
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@connect ser
Seraph
smoke123
@return
@return
@as god
set skill smokegod all 100
load obj 3349
give long hassan
force hassan wield long
cast bless hassan
@pulse 12
stat hassan
clone mob hassan
stat 1.hassan
stat 2.hassan
force 1.hassan remove long
stat 1.hassan
force 2.hassan remove long
stat 2.hassan
@mob 3060 3001
load obj 3043
set obj ring cost 2000
give ring cityguard
force cityguard wear ring
trust seraph 55
stat cityguard
@as ser
clone cityguard
@as god
stat 1.cityguard
stat 2.cityguard
force 1.cityguard remove ring
